(1\) const int* p \(or int const* p\): Pointer to constant integer. The integer data being pointed to cannot be altered through p \(*p =) Tj
T* (10 is illegal\), but p itself can be redirected to point to another address \(p = &y is legal\).) Tj
T* (2\) int* const p: Constant pointer to mutable integer. The address stored inside p cannot be changed \(p = &y is illegal\), but the) Tj
T* (integer value at that address may be modified \(*p = 10 is legal\).) Tj
T* (3\) const int* const p: Constant pointer to constant integer. Neither the targeted value \(*p = 10\) nor the target address \(p = &y\)) Tj
T* (may ever be modified.) Tj
